      "statusChangeID": "679d0c336eb16d9654afae3e",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nVRChat has utilized multithreading for quite a long time (since Unity 5.3 in 2017 and potentially earlier). You can observe this by launching VRChat and launching Task Manager, and watch how many physical/logical cores increase in load as the application launches and runs.\n\nOver time, we have implemented improvements and changes on top of Unity's implementations to further spread the work across available cores (PhysBones, VRCConstraints, etc), and we continue to address pain points as they come up.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-01-31T07:37:48.283Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Can we please implement multi-threading to the game? This would be a nice feature because it spreads the load among the entire cpu rather than just a couple threads. Multi threading will help with frame issues on all types of CPU's.  My gpu in a world with a few people will draw 300+ watts. but in a world with 10+ people and beyond, that goes down and my frames take a hit because the cpu cant keep up.",
